  "slug": "as-of-july-2026-what-is-the-financial-bankruptcy-s-a2a40c4c",
  "query": "As of July 2026, what is the financial/bankruptcy status of Beyond Meat Inc? Has it filed for Chapter 11 or restructured debt? Any bankruptcy warnings, going concern doubts, debt restructuring, or imminent bankruptcy risk in 2025-2026?",
  "answer": "I've completed the research. Here's the summary:\n\n**Beyond Meat, Inc. (NASDAQ: BYND) — Status as of July 2026:**\n\n**No Chapter 11 filing** — the company has explicitly denied filing or planning to file for bankruptcy. Instead, it pursued an **out-of-court debt restructuring** to avoid it:\n\n- **Sept–Dec 2025 debt exchange:** Swapped ~$1.15B of 0% Convertible Notes due 2027 for up to $202.5M of 7.00% Secured Second Lien PIK notes due 2030 + ~326M shares. ~97% of noteholders participated, cutting net debt by **>$800M** and extending maturities to 2030 — at the cost of **~5x dilution** (share count rose from ~76M to ~455M).\n- **Q1 2026 financials:** Revenue $58.2M (down 15.3% YoY), net loss –$28.5M, cash/restricted cash $205.8M, debt ~$411.6M, and a **stockholders' deficit of –$21.1M** (negative equity). Cash burn improved to $11.8M.\n- **Nasdaq delisting risk:** March 2026 warning for sub-$1 trading; compliance deadline **Aug 31, 2026**; reverse-split authority in place. Stock at **$0.59** (July 17, 2026), down ~92% from its 52-week high.\n- **Red flags:** Delayed 2025 10-K (filed April 9, 2026), disclosed **material weakness** in internal controls, restructuring officer hired, and ongoing analyst Chapter 11 warnings.\n\n**Verdict:** Not bankrupt, but acutely distressed — it chose a dilutive out-of-court restructuring over bankruptcy in late 2025, with continued analyst warnings of Chapter 11 risk if the turnaround (targeting positive adjusted EBITDA in H2 2026) fails.\n\nNote: AskNews tools were unavailable (subscription inactive), so findings rely on web search of financial news, SEC filings, and company IR releases, cross-validated with the financial data API.",
